00:04:43.101 --> 00:04:48.261
Orion stays on SLS for the climb off Earth because the engineering reality is a crew stack

00:04:48.261 --> 00:04:50.141
built around one vehicle's loads.

00:04:50.561 --> 00:04:54.581
Not a capsule you can move to another booster without starting the safety case over.

00:04:55.181 --> 00:04:59.701
The crew module, the service module, and the abort tower were designed as a single unit

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:05.221
whose structural loads, separation planes, and thermal protection needs match the interim

00:05:05.221 --> 00:05:10.821
cryogenic propulsion stage adapter. Swap the launch vehicle and you redesign the abort motors,

00:05:11.361 --> 00:05:16.081
the O-Give fairing panels, those curved nose pieces that take the aerodynamic heat,

00:05:16.561 --> 00:05:21.401
and the diaphragm that keeps hydrogen gas off Orion. None of which have been qualified on

00:05:21.401 --> 00:05:26.921
another booster. That diaphragm exists because SLS's upper stage burns liquid hydrogen,

00:05:27.441 --> 00:05:32.941
and hydrogen's molecular mass is two. The smallest molecule there is, so it leaks through seals

00:05:32.941 --> 00:05:38.621
that easily hold kerosene or methane, and it can embrittle metal. A barrier is the practical answer.

00:05:39.221 --> 00:05:45.881
The same Orion stage adapter can host up to 17 cube sats in mixed 6u and 12u sizes after the

00:05:45.881 --> 00:05:53.021
primary stack is clear of the atmosphere. A 6u is roughly 10 x 20 x 30cm, built from the textbook

00:05:53.021 --> 00:05:59.881
10cm 1u cell. Starships payload bay and ferring geometry are different, so an Orion adapter would

00:05:59.881 --> 00:06:05.001
need new load paths, meaning new routes for force through the structure, new avionics

00:06:05.001 --> 00:06:10.721
interfaces, and a new abort trajectory analysis. NASA's reference documents therefore keep

00:06:10.721 --> 00:06:16.221
SLS as the Earth to orbit stage for Orion, and have Starship do the Transluner injection.

00:06:16.741 --> 00:06:21.941
The burn toward the Moon after the two-dock in orbit. That burn from low Earth orbit takes

00:06:21.941 --> 00:06:27.261
on the order of 3 kilometers per second of extra speed. A textbook figure, which is

00:06:27.261 --> 00:06:31.161
a high-energy stage or a refueled starship sits in the architecture at all.

00:06:31.781 --> 00:06:36.421
The split keeps the existing abort system and avoids re-qualifying the crew module for

00:06:36.421 --> 00:06:39.801
a different vibration spectrum and a different acceleration curve.

00:06:40.381 --> 00:06:45.161
The launch abort system motors work in milliseconds to pull the crew module clear during a scent,

