and a jettison motor then throws the tower away once the vehicle is above most of the atmosphere,

00:06:50.921 --> 00:06:52.661
on the order of 100 kilometers up.

00:06:52.661 --> 00:06:57.201
up. Those motors and their mounting points were never sized for starships thrust curve

00:06:57.201 --> 00:07:02.461
or vibration spectrum, and the physics of why that matters as a race. The tower has to

00:07:02.461 --> 00:07:07.641
out accelerate the booster. Acceleration is force over mass, a different thrust versus

00:07:07.641 --> 00:07:12.461
time history changes the G-load on the crew, and the distance the capsule travels in those

00:07:12.461 --> 00:07:17.561
same milliseconds. A booster that spikes hard at ignition needs a tower that pulls harder

00:07:17.561 --> 00:07:22.681
and sooner. A booster that throttles deep on liquid engines has a smoother curve, and

00:07:22.681 --> 00:07:27.761
the old clearance analysis does not carry over. Peak aerodynamic pressure is half the

00:07:27.761 --> 00:07:32.981
air density times speed squared, so a fatter, slower, or steeper booster hits a different

00:07:32.981 --> 00:07:38.861
max queue, and the O-Give panels are sized for the old number, not the new one. Vibration

00:07:38.861 --> 00:07:44.041
